      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asbury%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Asbury Historic District, which surrounds Hutchinson, entered the National Register of Historic Places in 1993 for its architecture, industry, religion, community development, politics, and commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asbury%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hoffman Grist Mill, a historic landmark within the district, now hosts programs by the Musconetcong Watershed Association that celebrate the area’s social, agricultural, and industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asbury%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Along the Musconetcong River, the Plenge Archaeological Site in Hutchinson is one of only two major Paleo‑Indian sites in New Jersey, revealing the region’s ancient past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
